### Master development directive — Aethwyrd V9

The following is a proposed implementation brief, not a claim about the current repository's existing systems.

# AETHWYRD V9 — CINEMATIC STORYTELLING, AUDIO & IMMERSION

## Project Objective

Develop Aethwyrd V9 as a major single-player immersion and presentation upgrade.

The objective is to transform the presentation of Aethwyrd through cinematic storytelling, expressive characters, dynamic music, advanced sound design, environmental atmosphere, interactive cinematic events, and photo mode.

V9 must integrate with the existing architecture and preserve all established gameplay systems.

## 1. Mandatory Project Rules

- Aethwyrd is strictly a single-player game.
- Do not introduce multiplayer, online co-op, PvP, matchmaking, guilds, or network-dependent gameplay.
- Preserve existing gameplay functionality.
- Do not unnecessarily replace existing systems.
- Inspect the repository and identify the actual engine, architecture, and existing systems before implementation.
- Reuse existing character, animation, dialogue, audio, and world systems wherever possible.
- Keep systems modular and maintainable.
- Prioritize performance and stability.
- All new systems must be testable and documented.

## 2. Cinematic Director

Develop a cinematic presentation framework featuring:
- Dynamic camera positioning.
- Camera transitions.
- Character framing.
- Dialogue camera presets.
- Cutscene sequences.
- Boss introductions.
- Environmental establishing shots.
- Gameplay-to-cinematic transitions.
- Scene event triggers.

## 3. Advanced Dialogue Presentation

Implement:
- Facial expressions.
- Eye tracking.
- Blinking.
- Lip synchronization.
- Character gestures.
- Emotional reactions.
- Companion dialogue reactions.
- Dialogue animation blending.
- Voice profile integration.

## 4. Dynamic Music

Develop an adaptive music framework supporting:
- Exploration.
- Combat.
- Boss encounters.
- Dungeons.
- Emotional scenes.
- Regional themes.
- Companion themes.
- Smooth music transitions.
- Intensity-based music layers.

## 5. Environmental Sound

Implement:
- 3D positional audio.
- Terrain-dependent footsteps.
- Weather audio.
- Creature ambience.
- Cave and dungeon acoustics.
- Interior and exterior audio behavior.
- Environmental sound propagation.
- Magical sound effects.

## 6. Character Animation

Improve:
- Locomotion blending.
- Motion matching where supported.
- Contextual animations.
- Facial animation.
- Cinematic performance.
- Character-specific idle behaviors.
- Companion interactions.
- Natural transitions between gameplay states.

## 7. Environmental Presentation

Implement:
- Improved atmospheric lighting.
- Volumetric fog where supported.
- Weather presentation.
- Environmental particles.
- Water and reflection improvements.
- Day/night atmosphere.
- Location-specific visual effects.
- Story-dependent environmental changes.

## 8. Interactive Cinematic Events

Create reusable tools for:
- Scripted environmental sequences.
- Interactive escape sequences.
- Exploration discoveries.
- Companion-assisted scenes.
- Boss introductions.
- World events.
- Contextual player interactions.

Keep interactive events compatible with normal gameplay and avoid taking control away from the player unnecessarily.

## 9. Photo Mode

Implement:
- Free camera.
- Camera rotation.
- Camera distance.
- Field of view.
- Depth of field.
- Exposure.
- Time-of-day adjustment.
- Weather controls.
- Character and companion poses.
- Interface visibility toggle.
- Screenshot functionality.

## 10. Audio Production Tools

Create developer tools for:
- Dialogue asset management.
- Voice line organization.
- Audio importing.
- Missing audio validation.
- Lip-sync preview.
- Subtitle synchronization.
- Music event configuration.
- Audio mixing.
- Sound effect preview.

## 11. Accessibility

Provide:
- Subtitle customization.
- Adjustable text size.
- Camera shake controls.
- Motion blur controls.
- Separate audio volume controls.
- Color accessibility options.
- Dialogue speed controls.
- Cinematic skip settings.

## 12. Integration Requirements

Integrate V9 with:
- V3: Blender assets, character rigs, animation and production pipeline.
- V4: World state, quests, NPC routines and narrative events.
- V5: Combat animations, enemy reactions and boss presentations.
- V6: Crafting and interaction animations.
- V7: Dungeon discoveries, archaeology and ancient civilization sequences.
- V8: Companion expressions, reactions, creature animations and mounts.

Do not duplicate existing systems. Extend them through clearly defined interfaces.

## 13. Developer Tools

Create:
- Cinematic sequence editor.
- Camera preview tools.
- Dialogue preview tools.
- Lip-sync validation.
- Audio event debugger.
- Animation preview.
- Photo mode testing tools.
- Performance monitoring.
- Missing asset detection.

## 14. Testing Requirements

Test:
- Camera transitions.
- Dialogue synchronization.
- Facial animation.
- Audio playback.
- Music transitions.
- Environmental sound.
- Cinematic interruption and recovery.
- Companion scene integration.
- Performance in large environments.
- Accessibility settings.
- Save/load compatibility.

## 15. Final Objective

Deliver Aethwyrd V9 as a cohesive cinematic immersion upgrade.

The player should experience a world with expressive characters, memorable scenes, beautiful environments, atmospheric audio, and cinematic moments that complement gameplay.

Maintain the identity of Aethwyrd as a complete, strictly single-player fantasy adventure.

